const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 1 Level 5 Walkthrough: Yacht";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 1 Level 5 walkthrough: the code 58137 on the life vest, the keypad it opens, the four jars of coloured sand, the bar shelves you have to sort, and the finish worth +50 coins.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the keypad code in Chapter 1 Level 5?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "58137. The digits are printed in a vertical column on the left panel of the orange life vest on the aft wall, next to a red anchor and a blue anchor. Take the vest into your inventory, press Examine, read the digits top to bottom and type them into the steel keypad beside the stairs."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where do the four jars of coloured sand come from?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Red sand comes out of the cabinet under the wash-corner counter once the five pump bottles are worked in the right order. Green and blue sand are picked up in the same run along the shelf wall with the sailboat picture and the ship's bell. White sand comes out of the round aquarium on the deck after you use the claw toy in it. The game stacks all four into a single jar in your inventory."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "In what order do you pour the sand into the empty jar?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Blue first, then the cream layer, then red, then green on top. That is the order our recording pours them and the game accepts it. Read from the bottom of the finished jar upwards, the stripes are blue, cream, red, green."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do you solve the bar bottle shelves?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It is a sorting puzzle, not a code. The three shelves hold bottles in green, red and pale blue, and each shelf has to end up holding one colour: green on top, red in the middle, pale blue on the bottom. When the last bottle moves, the shelves release the next item."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the reward for finishing the Yacht?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "+50 coins. The level ends in the lounge after the piano beat, with the photographs on the keys and the line about the old amusement park."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does the Yacht have a timed puzzle?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. The clock in the corner is the level clock counting up, not a countdown, and nothing in the level fails you for being slow. The only thing that can hold you up is the pump-bottle sequence on the wash counter."}}]};
